53
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:17,500
We can't just stand here, let's find them!

54
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,000
No!

55
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,240
Hey, tell me, is Gen through the bomber?

56
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,020
I... I don't know

57
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:24,000
Sorry

58
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,740
But he did go like this with his hand and

59
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:28,780
Blew the head off the guy I was with!

60
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:33,560
A power that is clearly meant specifically for murder

61
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:36,940
So he's no stranger to fighting battles, that much is obvious

62
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:40,240
It would be unwise to try to fight them head on

63
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,340
We have to!

64
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:44,480
Sir, they took at least five different card types from us!

65
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,520
Just think about it!

66
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:47,380
They could have completed their collection!

67
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:50,520
Now list on, card number two

68
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:57,680
It looks like they still haven't found number two, strip of beach

69
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:59,760
We're all right for the time being

70
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:04,800
Our immediate priority is to find the number two card before they can get to it

71
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,760
Well, we still have our exchange voucher for Angel's Breath

72
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:08,880
It is possible

73
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,000
You're right!

74
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,700
Let's get out there and find it!

75
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:13,220
Accompany on!

76
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,660
To Sofrabi!

77
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:23,080
Congratulations! We did it!

78
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,480
The risky dice and levy combination really paid off

79
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,240
We're at 93 types!

80
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:31,720
No, we used one up to change those guys' faces, remember?

81
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,020
So we're right at 92

82
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:37,060
But the important thing is that we took the cards they were monopolizing

83
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:40,740
And for two of the other ones, we're just waiting for someone to use gain on them

84
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:43,480
The biggest obstacle for us now is number two

85
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:47,260
Good point, but at least we know that it's somewhere in Sofrabi

86
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:52,320
Right, then we'll go after 72, 21, and 9, all in that order

87
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:55,320
And then we'll head to Sofrabi to find number two

88
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:59,940
For 75, we'll just find someone who has it and take it from them

89
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:03,400
I think it's time we started thinking

90
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:08,160
About the three specified slot cards that we each want to keep

91
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:11,100
And how to spend our 50 billion

92
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:14,060
Hey, Killua

93
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:16,860
There's something that's been bugging me lately

94
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:17,460
Yeah?

95
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:20,240
There are hundreds of players in this game, aren't there?

96
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:24,260
But in spite of that, we've been able to turn every item we've obtained into cards

97
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:25,400
And that's weird, right?

98
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,500
Wait, what do you mean?

99
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:29,160
You can only convert a card so many times

100
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:32,380
And even B-rank specified slot types have a 30-card limit

101
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:36,860
I would have thought that the players here before us would have already collected them, you know?

102
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,380
I guess that's true

103
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,720
But there is one other way you can look at it

104
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,960
Not that many teams here can make real progress

105
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,320
Maybe fewer than 30

106
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,020
Oh, yeah, I get it

107
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:52,840
See, most of the players don't seem to be all that worried about getting specified slot cards

108
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:56,600
Best I can tell, they're just struggling to find a way out of the game

109
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:01,200
It'd suck if you got to Masadora and couldn't find any leave cards there

110
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:02,360
Sure would

111
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,280
That's why

112
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:07,500
That's it

113
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:08,700
What?

114
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:13,520
If you guys got to Masadora and there weren't any leave cards there, what would you do?

115
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,400
Well, let me think

116
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:19,360
I'd save up some money and wait until another leave card showed up

117
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:19,840
Yup

118
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:24,860
Okay, so then what if you acquired a super rare spell card while you were there waiting?

119
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:28,500
I guess I would just sell it and buy more spell cards until a leave came in

120
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:29,140
Really?

121
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:30,020
Huh?

122
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,980
Because I would definitely save it

123
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:35,660
Wouldn't it be awful if all the cards you bought ended up being worthless?

124
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:39,880
If you saved it, maybe you could trade up for a leave, but

125
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:43,160
Well

126
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:48,980
Hmm

127
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:52,640
Need a leave?

128
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:55,440
You want to go back home?

129
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:57,200
I think we can help you

130
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:12,440
Okay, now we've got four specified slot cards for three leaves

131
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:15,520
Yeah, making a total of 54 types in all

132
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:16,480
Score!

133
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:20,860
All right

134
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:24,900
All of the cards that wouldn't fit in our binders have reverted into items

135
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:27,940
Looks like we're running out of free slots pretty fast

136
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:29,980
We should probably organize them

137
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:34,600
We've got 135 free slots between the three of us

138
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:37,500
So we should each leave five slots free

139
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,040
How about you keep the spell cards, Killua?

140
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:42,540
Biski needs a few defensive ones

141
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:43,620
Hold on

142
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:45,160
I have to use spell cards?

143
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,080
No way!

144
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,460
Those are far too confusing

145
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,200
Then study!

146
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:49,220
What the hell?

147
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,160
Okay

148
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,880
Book

149
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:57,800
So up to this point, we've been deliberately avoiding the other players

150
00:08:57,800 --> 00:09:01,500
But now, there are certain cards we really need

151
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,420
So we'll have to take some risks

152
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:07,800
Well, I suggest we get all that we can ourselves

153
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:11,380
And then actively negotiate with other players we meet on the way

154
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:12,840
That sound good to you?

155
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,080
I'm in

156
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:14,860
Yeah!

157
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:17,700
See ya

158
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,280
Wait a second

159
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:24,320
This card is worthless

160
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:26,140
It's just a transformed fake

161
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:28,960
Oh wow, I'm really sorry about that

162
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,960
Here's the real one

163
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:34,400
You can't trust any of these guys, huh?

164
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:36,000
We better stay on the defensive

165
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,120
No joke

166
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:39,140
We're lucky he has that necklace

167
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:41,060
It certainly comes in handy

168
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:45,300
Okay, I got a question

169
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:48,420
This necklace is supposed to be able to remove curses, right?

170
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,820
From spell cards

171
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:51,140
But not any others

172
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:53,260
Oh, guess it won't work then

173
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,120
What, you have an idea, Gon?

174
00:09:55,560 --> 00:10:00,520
I was just wondering if maybe a curse was behind the disease those villagers were suffering from

175
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,320
What villagers?

176
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:05,500
Oh, I remember those guys

177
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:08,520
The ones who took all your money, right?

178
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:12,380
I doubt that would work because they're not cards

179
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:13,080
Right

180
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:16,040
But still, it might be worth a shot

181
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:22,000
It's a lot to ask

182
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,840
But will you trust us with your lives?

183
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:32,620
You gave us everything you had without even the slightest hint of hesitation

184
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:34,860
Yes, we trust you

185
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:35,680
Yes, we trust you

186
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:48,240
It worked!

187
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:52,480
Thank you all very much

188
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:55,880
This treasure has been passed down for many generations

189
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:58,280
Please accept it

190
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:00,900
It worked!

191
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:04,060
We got a wild luck Alexandrite!

192
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:04,900
Heck yeah!

193
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:13,200
Attention, another player has cast contact on you

194
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:15,700
Hey, this is Kazu

195
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,960
Could you and I meet in person?

196
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:19,920
I really have to talk to you

197
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:20,820
About what?

198
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:23,580
A team is close to clearing the game

199
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:28,440
A three-man team led by someone named Genthru

200
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:30,060
Genthru

201
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:42,320
Thanks for taking the time to come out, everyone

202
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:45,240
As I mentioned via contact

203
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:48,400
Team Genthru is getting very close to completing the game

204
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,480
I just checked the ranking

205
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,740
And they're currently at 96 types

206
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:55,300
We have to come up with a strategy

207
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,060
And now

208
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:58,040
I've got a question

209
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:58,680
Yeah

210
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:01,000
How exactly do you check the rankings?

211
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,300
Oh, well

212
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,720
Great, you don't even know how to do that

213
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:06,880
We don't have time to explain the whole game to them

214
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:09,280
So just cut to the chase, alright?

215
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:11,120
There's no need to be mean

216
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:13,280
All of us are here to exchange information

217
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,580
He's right, Asta

218
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:15,580
You never know

219
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:18,040
These kids just might have a bit of intel you don't

220
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,380
That's impossible

221
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,120
Hmm?

222
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,620
They're rank amateurs

223
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:23,720
Who don't even know how to use the trade shop

224
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,860
Don't make me laugh

225
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:26,720
In the trade shop

226
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:29,980
You can look at the official rankings of who has the most cards

227
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:31,240
Which can be really useful

228
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,980
And if you pay a fee

229
00:12:32,980 --> 00:12:35,680
Then they'll even tell you which specific cards they have

230
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:39,640
But just because you can get a player's name from the ranking

231
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:42,620
Doesn't mean you can use contact or fluoroscopy

232
00:12:42,620 --> 00:12:44,540
You gotta meet him for that

233
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:47,620
Do you feel a little smarter now?

234
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:48,660
Little boy?

235
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:53,600
Thing is, if we know all of the members on the team

236
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:56,620
We can determine exactly how many cards they have between them

237
00:12:56,620 --> 00:12:59,480
And Team Genthrou is only missing

238
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:03,620
Numbers 0, 2, 9, and 75 in all

239
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:04,800
75, huh?

240
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:09,800
There's a well-accepted theory that number 0 only appears in an event

241
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,640
After the other 99 are collected

242
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,180
So they only need three

243
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:15,480
What we're proposing is this

244
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:19,260
We find one of those three types before they do and monopolize it

245
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:21,020
Preventing them from clearing the game

246
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,340
Really? That's it?

247
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:27,000
I figured we could at least inundate them with spell cards or something

248
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,120
We've learned that they already obtained a Paladin's necklace

249
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,800
So Levy is the only spell that might work

250
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:34,400
And they can block it

251
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,460
If certain conditions are met anyway

252
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:41,640
Let's assume that Genthrou is willing to reveal the fact that they have 96 types

253
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:45,760
Because they've got all their pages protected with Fortress

254
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:47,060
It's possible

255
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:51,100
And Genthrou was hoarding a bunch of spell cards

256
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:53,600
Him and the other guys who try to recruit us

257
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,480
So it makes a lot of sense

258
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:58,580
Well, we could always take their cards by force

259
00:13:58,580 --> 00:14:00,820
Would you be willing to lead the attack?

260
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:04,560
Who knows what other abilities that three-man team has to offer?

261
00:14:06,460 --> 00:14:10,640
The most practical plan is to find a card type to monopolize

262
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:12,640
No objections, I assume?

263
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,760
Then let's get down to business

264
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:18,640
We're gonna need everyone here working together

265
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,260
All that sounds good to me

266
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:22,940
But these new members are a problem

267
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:24,140
Hold on, Asta

268
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:26,560
Each team satisfies the prerequisite

269
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,720
All of them hold more than 50 cards

270
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:32,280
Just like you insisted to begin with

271
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,640
Yeah, maybe so

272
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:37,680
But I also insisted that they had to be people who could contribute, right?

273
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:42,780
I failed to see how either of these little kids are gonna contribute anything

274
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:46,060
The only one here not contributing so far is you

275
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:48,160
Well, at least you're a big talker

276
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,480
But I'm still not sure you can be useful

277
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,780
So let's see some proof

278
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:54,160
We know Team Gethrou's abilities

279
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,460
And there are three cards they're missing

280
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,460
We have one of them

281
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:01,840
Hmph, still got a problem?

282
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,380
That's good enough for me

283
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:06,380
So these abilities, what are they exactly?

284
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:07,720
Hold on

285
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:10,500
Let's see some proof that you can be useful to us

286
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:11,960
Because I doubt it

287
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:15,240
71 types of specified slot cards

288
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,880
That's a hell of a lot more than you have

289
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:20,040
How about I give you an A rank

290
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,740
In return for a little information

291
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:24,700
Is that good enough?

292
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,040
No, it isn't

293
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,780
We can get those ourselves

294
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:28,900
No big deal

295
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,740
If you want us to tell you anything

296
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:32,740
You can give us two S rank cards

297
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:34,500
Or equally valuable information

298
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,080
Don't press your luck, you damn little brat

299
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,400
Hear that, everyone?

300
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:40,880
These kids won't be any help

301
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:43,500
They want two S rank cards from each team

302
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:44,480
Ten cards

303
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,480
Really?

304
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,740
Don't be stupid

305
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:48,340
I just meant your team

306
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,640
Huh?

307
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:52,340
I'm fine giving information to the others

308
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:55,040
They can decide what they want to give us in return

309
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,180
But you?

310
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:59,140
You guys get nothing unless you give me what I asked for

311
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:00,140
Ugh

312
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:03,980
Shoulda known a stupid brat would dwell on that silly argument

313
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,680
Would both of you knock it off?

314
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,740
Don't waste our time fighting with each other

315
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:10,740
Well I haven't agreed to team up with them yet

316
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:12,140
Master, it's fine

317
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:13,480
Just give him two cards

318
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,240
He's right

319
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,680
We've got to move past this

320
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:18,100
Look, I don't have a problem with giving them cards

321
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:19,700
It doesn't make a difference to me

322
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:21,500
He's the one trying to pick a fight

323
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:23,600
No, you are picking a fight

324
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,700
Come on guys, let's get out of here

325
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,840
I don't want to team up with these losers

326
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:30,040
I know how you feel, it's frustrating

327
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:31,900
It's just that given the circumstances

328
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:41,200
Okay, what we've been able to figure out so far is that Genthru's abilities are Countdown and Little Flower

329
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:44,780
